    board: file CF-074 — 20 of 22 complete rows have no resolvable closure evidence; correct CF-046
    
    The repository has a written closure doctrine (docs/traceability-doctrine.md rules 2/4/6)
    and no gate that enforces it: tests/selftest.sh section 7 parses the JSONL and stops
    there, and no script under scripts/ or tests/ validates detail.evidence.
    
    Measured at origin/main 64c0c10 in a throwaway clone (script and transcript reproduced in
    home/.hermes/stand-in/review/code-factory/review-2026-11-03-evidence.md, this tick's
    addendum): of 22 complete rows, exactly TWO (CF-034, CF-055) carry an evidence entry whose
    artifacts resolve in the published tree and whose tree_fp resolves to a git object. The
    other 20 do not, and the worst shape is shared: one fingerprint,
    59f476975880e46d49eec1fbaec75b289ced048f4e669855d2cee386061fb5ec, is pasted across eight
    closures (CF-009, CF-010, CF-014, CF-015, CF-030, CF-032, CF-033, CF-035) and
    `git cat-file -t` on it prints "fatal: Not a valid object name", with no document in the
    tree stating the algorithm that would regenerate it.
    
    CF-074 asks for the generator, not another instance: a committed audit script that exits
    nonzero while any complete row lacks a resolvable entry, wired into tests/selftest.sh with
    the pre-fix failure recorded. Individual instances already have rows (CF-045/046/047/059/
    067/073); one row per instance would leave the generator running.
    
    CF-046's note is corrected in place: it cited CF-032's run_id 0576a54e as "the published
    judge-verdict commit", but that object resolves only via the LOCAL ref
    refs/gitreins/history in the owner's checkout and is absent from a fresh clone — doctrine
    rule 4 disqualifies exactly that shape. Its dangling run_ids and the CF-037 open marker
    re-verified and still hold.
    
    Gates: `bash tests/selftest.sh` PASS at this tree; gitreins guard Tier 1 DEGRADED PASS
    (secrets clean, tests full PASS, lint skipped — no implementation files staged), the
    documented board-only outcome. Board-only diff: 2 rows changed (CF-046 note, CF-074 new)
    plus one task_created event; 59 rows parse, no duplicate ids.
    
