 {"id":"CF-047","title":"docs/traceability-doctrine.md does not define the detail.evidence fields (run_id, tree_fp, artifacts) that every closed row uses","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"docs/traceability-doctrine.md (CF-012) defines the ch:trace marker fields but not the detail.evidence fields that every closed board row actually uses. The 2026-11-03 review sweep found two binding shapes among closed rows, neither documented: (a) proper git tree hashes — CF-032's tree_fp a3e9b7411d08670da83273b93189024a83e0fb30 is the git tree of the judged implementation commits 6f75e28/8f1e8c1 (git rev-parse 8f1e8c1^{tree} resolves it; run_id 0576a54e names the separate judge-verdict commit, whose own tree is 048fad50e6181dfaefa2ce15bbb838850b0846f8 because it adds the verdict artifact), and CF-040's tree_fp 4b97e25e4e41b51a07c5bd703a4887f102ffbbf5 is the git tree of commit 0959258; (b) 64-hex values that are not objects in this repository at all — CF-011/CF-013/CF-037/CF-038 (git cat-file -t fails on each). Nothing in the repository tells a stranger which commit's tree a tree_fp records, or that some values are not git objects at all, which is precisely what closure rule 6 exists to prevent. This row asks for the vocabulary to be defined, not for history to be rewritten. AMENDMENT 2026-11-03: an earlier revision of this row stated the resolution command as git rev-parse 0576a54e^{tree} equaling a3e9b741 — that command resolves the verdict commit's own tree (048fad50) and was wrong; the judge's 2026-11-03 spot-check (verdict bd4c1251) caught it and this text is the correction.","acceptance_criteria":"1. docs/traceability-doctrine.md gains a section defining run_id, tree_fp and artifacts for detail.evidence entries, each with a concrete resolution command; the section demonstrates the binding on CF-032: git rev-parse 8f1e8c1^{tree} yields a3e9b7411d08670da83273b93189024a83e0fb30 (the judged implementation tree the tree_fp records) while git rev-parse 0576a54e^{tree} yields 048fad50e6181dfaefa2ce15bbb838850b0846f8 (the verdict commit's own tree), and states explicitly which commit's tree a tree_fp records. 2. The section states which run_id shapes are legal (a published commit sha, or a named audit run whose record lives in a committed artifact), that tree_fp must be a git tree hash resolvable in this repository's object store, and that a value failing git cat-file -t is not evidence of a tree (the CF-011/CF-013/CF-037/CF-038 64-hex shape). 3. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.","created_at":"2026-11-03T10:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T10:40:00Z","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"code-factory-review-2026-11-03-09-10-28","ts":"2026-11-03T10:05:00Z","tree_fp":"none:doctrine-gap","artifacts":[]},{"run_id":"code-factory-review-2026-11-03-09-10-28-amend1","ts":"2026-11-03T10:40:00Z","tree_fp":"none:self-correction-judge-bd4c1251","artifacts":[]}]}}
 {"id":"PERF-012","title":"Selftest board validation is process-spawn bound: one python3 per row, 1.572 s -> 0.778 s at 30 rows","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured at origin/main 4638e90 using the tracked 30-row board (sha256 cfc42c9b2263a0b12e308786096d61ef6e4f161a8ca69680c8802fba6832ed22). tests/selftest.sh:150 validated the board with one python3 per JSONL row: strace -f -c on the unmodified script recorded wait4 669 calls / 1.805 s (82.3 percent) and execve 495. One-process parser measured paired and interleaved with hyperfine --warmup 3 --runs 15, both arms in one session: before 1.572 s mean, 0.249 s stddev, 1.309 s min, 2.153 s max, 15 runs, all exit 0; after 0.778 s mean, 0.125 s stddev, 0.653 s min, 1.123 s max, 15 runs, all exit 0; 2.02x. wait4 669 -> 576, execve 495 -> 465. Behaviour preserved: malformed line appended -> FAIL 30 of 31 in both arms; trailing newline stripped -> PASS 29/29 in both; empty board -> PASS 0/0 in both. Landed in 18b06cf with evidence docs/audits/code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-PERF-012.md and pushed to origin/main. Supersedes this row original 16-row numbers (591.5 ms -> 213.7 ms): the fixture grew 16 -> 30 rows and the script gained sections 4b and 10, so those magnitudes are not comparable; the mechanism is confirmed and the magnitude is the paired pair above.","acceptance_criteria":"1. tests/selftest.sh validates every board row with one parser process, not one python3 per row.\n2. bash tests/selftest.sh exits 0 and prints SELFTEST: PASS with 30/30 rows parse at origin/main.\n3. One malformed JSON line still makes bash tests/selftest.sh exit nonzero and print the parsed/total counts.\n4. An unterminated final line and an empty board keep the pre-change outcomes (PASS 29/29 and PASS 0/0).\n5. Paired hyperfine on the identical 30-row fixture reports before/after mean, stddev, min, max, run count and exit status, with the JSON artifacts kept.","created_at":"2026-11-03T11:52:37Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T11:52:37Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"c48792e1d89cff6d2a5b063be31e8734f0617d9a28e14a81ae29d99be07cb1b0","evidence":[{"run_id":"code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-10-56-35-selftest-board-30row","ts":"2026-11-03T11:52:37Z","tree_fp":"a7e996a21e8ce95cd01bf25d7652a2836f3b834a9e897c1d761219df6199245a","artifacts":["docs/audits/code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-PERF-012.md"]}]},"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"18b06cf854c0df6ea47774acc5f0998cd8e40bff","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"Board JSONL validation replaced 30 python3 launches with one parser process: paired hyperfine 1.572 s -> 0.778 s (2.02x), wait4 669 -> 576, selftest PASS 30/30; malformed-line, unterminated-tail and empty-board controls identical to the old loop.","completed_at":"2026-11-03T11:55:00Z"}
 {"id":"CF-048","title":"P4 — A board truncated mid-record still passes selftest: unterminated final line is never parsed","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Found while replacing the per-row parser in tests/selftest.sh:150 (PERF-012). The old loop was `while IFS= read -r line; do ... done < board`, and bash read returns nonzero at EOF without a trailing delimiter, so the body never runs for an unterminated final line. Measured at origin/main 4638e90 plus 18b06cf: strip the trailing newline from .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl (30 records, last one partial) and bash tests/selftest.sh prints PASS 29/29 and SELFTEST: PASS, i.e. a board truncated mid-record passes the only board check in CI. PERF-012 deliberately preserved this behaviour so its diff stayed a pure performance change. Reproduction: cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && cp .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl /tmp/b && perl -0pi -e \"s/\\n\\z//\" .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl && bash tests/selftest.sh | grep rows; cp /tmp/b .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl.","acceptance_criteria":"1. A board whose final record is not newline-terminated makes bash tests/selftest.sh exit nonzero and name the unterminated row count, proven by a fixture in tests/selftest.sh.\n2. The fixture can also go green: the same test passes on the intact board.\n3. The empty-board case keeps its documented outcome (PASS 0/0 or an explicit FAIL, whichever the fix chooses) and that choice is stated in tests/selftest.sh.\n4. bash tests/selftest.sh remains PASS and its runtime stays within 5 percent of the 0.778 s mean recorded in PERF-012 at the same 30-row fixture.","created_at":"2026-11-03T11:52:37Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T11:52:37Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"425c80f4bc2082bd58fa4a7373719edbf308926219fa80dc46cb3dd7b41325ca"},"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"completed_at":null}
